IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `qld-part08a-defined-terms`

-- Tests for Part 8, first group (qld-part08a-defined-terms.l4).
-- Each expected value was worked out by hand from the text, as cited.

§ `Tests of Part 8, ss 32 to 32F`

§§ `ss 32 to 32AB`

#ASSERT `the other part of speech or grammatical form has a corresponding meaning (s 32)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the other part of speech or grammatical form has a corresponding meaning (s 32)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the definition applies (s 32A)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- SAYS Definitions in or applicable to an Act apply except so far as the context or subject matter otherwise indicates or requires; once it does, s 32A does not settle the application (s 32A).
#ASSERT `the definition applies (s 32A)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the definition applies (s 32A)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the definition applies to the provision (s 32AA)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition applies to the provision (s 32AA)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- SAYS A non-exhaustive definition for another Act does not exclude or limit, but may extend, the meaning given by this Act's definition (s 32AB(c)).
#ASSERT `the non-exhaustive definition excludes or limits the meaning given by the Interpretation Act definition (s 32AB(c))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the non-exhaustive definition excludes or limits the meaning given by the Interpretation Act definition (s 32AB(c))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the non-exhaustive definition may extend the meaning given by the Interpretation Act definition (s 32AB(c))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the non-exhaustive definition may extend the meaning given by the Interpretation Act definition (s 32AB(c))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- SAYS If the two definitions, read in context, are inconsistent, the Interpretation Act definition is displaced (s 32AB(d)).
#ASSERT `the Interpretation Act definition is displaced (s 32AB(d))` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Interpretation Act definition is displaced (s 32AB(d))` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 32B to 32CB`

#ASSERT `the word includes each other gender (s 32B)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the word includes each other gender (s 32B)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the word includes the number asked about (s 32C)` singular plural EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the word includes the number asked about (s 32C)` plural singular EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the word includes the number asked about (s 32C)` singular singular EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the word includes the number asked about (s 32C)` plural plural EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `what the word indicates about the power (s 32CA(1) and (2))` `the word may, or a similar word or expression` EQUALS JUST `that the power may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion`
#ASSERT `what the word indicates about the power (s 32CA(1) and (2))` `the word must, or a similar word or expression` EQUALS JUST `that the power is required to be exercised`
#ASSERT `what the word indicates about the power (s 32CA(1) and (2))` `another word` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): an Act passed after 1 January 1992.
#ASSERT `s 32CA applies to the Act despite any presumption or rule of interpretation (s 32CA(3))` (Date 2 1 1992) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 32CA applies to the Act despite any presumption or rule of interpretation (s 32CA(3))` (Date 1 1 1992) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `words and expressions used in the Act have the same meanings as they have in the other law (s 32CB(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `words and expressions used in the Act have the same meanings as they have in the other law (s 32CB(1))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 32CB(1) limits s 22 (s 32CB(2))` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 32D`

#ASSERT `a reference to a person generally includes a reference to the entity (s 32D(1))` TRUE `a corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a person generally includes a reference to the entity (s 32D(1))` TRUE `an individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a person generally includes a reference to the entity (s 32D(1))` TRUE `anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to a person generally includes a reference to the entity (s 32D(1))` FALSE `a corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsection (1) is displaced merely because of an express reference to either an individual or a corporation elsewhere in the Act (s 32D(2))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) is displaced merely because of an express reference to either an individual or a corporation elsewhere in the Act (s 32D(2))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The three example lists, word by word.
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "another" EQUALS JUST `a reference to a person generally`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "anyone" EQUALS JUST `a reference to a person generally`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "no-one" EQUALS JUST `a reference to a person generally`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "one" EQUALS JUST `a reference to a person generally`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "party" EQUALS JUST `a reference to a person generally`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "person" EQUALS JUST `a reference to a person generally`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "someone" EQUALS JUST `a reference to a person generally`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "whoever" EQUALS JUST `a reference to a person generally`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "body corporate" EQUALS JUST `an express reference to a corporation`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "company" EQUALS JUST `an express reference to a corporation`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "corporation sole" EQUALS JUST `an express reference to a corporation`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "adult" EQUALS JUST `an express reference to an individual`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "child" EQUALS JUST `an express reference to an individual`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "spouse" EQUALS JUST `an express reference to an individual`
#ASSERT `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` "tenant" EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 32DA`

-- SAYS Two persons are de facto partners if they live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis and are neither married to each other nor related by family (s 32DA(1)).
#ASSERT `each of the 2 persons is a de facto partner of the other (s 32DA(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `each of the 2 persons is a de facto partner of the other (s 32DA(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `each of the 2 persons is a de facto partner of the other (s 32DA(1))` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `each of the 2 persons is a de facto partner of the other (s 32DA(1))` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `the nature and extent of their common residence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `the length of their relationship` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `whether or not a sexual relationship exists or existed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangement for financial support` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `their ownership, use and acquisition of property` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `the degree of mutual commitment to a shared life, including the care and support of each other` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `the care and support of children` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `the performance of household tasks` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `the reputation and public aspects of their relationship` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "any of their circumstances": a circumstance that is not listed may be taken into account too.
#ASSERT `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` `any other circumstance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a particular finding in relation to any circumstance is necessary in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(3))` EQUALS FALSE
-- SAYS Two persons are not to be regarded as living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis only because they have a common residence (s 32DA(4)).
#ASSERT `the 2 persons are regarded as living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(4))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the 2 persons are regarded as living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(4))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the gender of the persons is relevant for s 32DA(1) (s 32DA(5)(a))` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the person is related by family to the other person (s 32DA(5)(b))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person is related by family to the other person (s 32DA(5)(b))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a reference to a spouse includes a reference to a de facto partner as defined in s 32DA (s 32DA(6))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a spouse includes a reference to a de facto partner as defined in s 32DA (s 32DA(6))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to a spouse includes a reference to a de facto partner as defined in s 32DA (s 32DA(6))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 32E and 32F`

#ASSERT `the requirement obliges the person to produce or make available a document reproducing the information in a form capable of being understood (s 32E(c))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirement obliges the person to produce or make available a document reproducing the information in a form capable of being understood (s 32E(c))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the requirement obliges the person to produce or make available a document reproducing the information in a form capable of being understood (s 32E(c))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the production of the document in that form complies with the requirement (s 32E(d))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the production of the document in that form complies with the requirement (s 32E(d))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): the time an Act or provision comes into operation.
#ASSERT `the first moment is the same instant as the second moment` (`the time a reference to commencement refers to (s 32F(1))` (`the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2025))) (`the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2025))
-- (2) and its example: section 24(3) says "This section expires 1 month after the commencement": the commencement of section 24(3).
-- src:648 | Example of subsection (2)—
-- src:649 | If section 24(3) of an Act stated ‘This section expires 1 month after the commencement’, ‘the commencement’ referred to is the commencement of section 24(3).
@ref s 32F(2), example (src:648-649)
#ASSERT `what a reference to the commencement refers to (s 32F(2))` FALSE EQUALS `the commencement of the provision in which the reference occurs`
#ASSERT `what a reference to the commencement refers to (s 32F(2))` TRUE EQUALS `the commencement of the Act or provision indicated`
